  "security_implications": "Key unmasking: The gen_key_unmask block XORs two key shares to produce an unmasked key. An incomplete assignment (only bit 0 written) would corrupt key material. Entropy readiness: gating entropy_ready with a write qualifier (qe) can disable the entropy source, stalling KMAC or causing it to operate with insufficient entropy, weakening cryptographic strength and randomness. Hash counter always-enabled write creates a risk that software reads a constantly toggling counter, making entropy-health monitoring unreliable. All these can directly compromise the integrity and security of the KMAC operation.",
  "evidence_refs": [
    "kmac.sv:513-556"
  ],
